codex
The caller trace confirms the fix can stay within existing architecture: `finish_block_break` captures the original `BlockState`, invokes the live `broken` hook after removal, and passes that old state into it. I’ll make the turtle decrement derive from `args.state` (and from the pre-step/fall state), so the post-removal hook reproduces vanilla `playerDestroy` without inventing a new public API or misusing `player_will_destroy`.
