codex
Classification is now clear enough to make a live edit: `FunctionCommand.modifySenderForExecution` is the one behavioral gap. Vanilla suppresses output for commands dispatched from a function (`FunctionCommand.java:106-108`), while Pumpkin currently re-dispatches function lines with the original source. I’m wiring suppression into the existing `DatapackManager::execute_function` call path and adding a small unit test; the other leads map to existing hooks, generated state data, inline logic, or client-only behavior.
